DECLARE `How an entry defines` IS ONE OF
    `by saying what the term means`
    `by saying what the term includes`
    `by saying what the term means, as the context requires`
    `by pointing at another enactment`
    `by saying what the term refers to`
    `by saying how a reference is to be construed`

-- The bracket at the end of an entry: a year, a date, nothing, or (the paragraph on relationships) a date that the bracket describes and does not give.
DECLARE `Mark of a Schedule 1 entry` IS ONE OF
    `the entry has no mark`
    `the entry has a year` HAS `the year in the bracket` IS A NUMBER
    `the entry has a date` HAS `the date in the bracket` IS A DATE
    `the entry has a date described but not given` HAS `the words in the bracket` IS A STRING

DECLARE `A Schedule 1 definition` HAS
    `the terms it defines`       IS A LIST OF STRING
    `how it defines`             IS A `How an entry defines`
    `in relation to`             IS A MAYBE STRING
    `what the entry says`        IS A STRING
    `the enactment it points at` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the mark`                   IS A `Mark of a Schedule 1 entry`

