-- src:337 | In relation to England and Wales—
-- src:338 | (a) “indictable offence” means an offence which, if committed by an adult, is triable on indictment, whether it is exclusively so triable or triable either way;
-- src:339 | (b) “summary offence” means an offence which, if committed by an adult, is triable only summarily;
-- src:340 | (c) “offence triable either way” means an offence , other than an offence triable on indictment only by virtue of Part V of the Criminal Justice Act 1988 which, if committed by an adult, is triable either on indictment or summarily;
-- src:341 | and the terms “indictable”, “summary” and “triable either way”, in their application to offences, are to be construed accordingly.
-- src:342 | In the above definitions references to the way or ways in which an offence is triable are to be construed without regard to the effect, if any, of section 22 of the Magistrates’ Courts Act 1980 on the mode of trial in a particular case.
-- src:343 | In relation to a term of imprisonment in respect of an offence triable either way under the law of England and Wales, “general limit in a magistrates’ court” means the limit laid down in respect of the offence by section 224(1) of the Sentencing Code (as it has effect from time to time).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, Offences (England and Wales) (src:337-343)
GIVETH A `A Schedule 1 definition`
`Schedule 1 states Offences (England and Wales)` MEANS
    `A Schedule 1 definition` WITH
        `the terms it defines`       IS (LIST "indictable offence", "summary offence", "offence triable either way", "indictable", "summary", "triable either way", "general limit in a magistrates’ court")
        `how it defines`             IS `by saying what the term means`
        `in relation to`             IS (JUST "In relation to England and Wales")
        `what the entry says`        IS "In relation to England and Wales— (a) “indictable offence” means an offence which, if committed by an adult, is triable on indictment, whether it is exclusively so triable or triable either way; (b) “summary offence” means an offence which, if committed by an adult, is triable only summarily; (c) “offence triable either way” means an offence , other than an offence triable on indictment only by virtue of Part V of the Criminal Justice Act 1988 which, if committed by an adult, is triable either on indictment or summarily; and the terms “indictable”, “summary” and “triable either way”, in their application to offences, are to be construed accordingly. In the above definitions references to the way or ways in which an offence is triable are to be construed without regard to the effect, if any, of section 22 of the Magistrates’ Courts Act 1980 on the mode of trial in a particular case. In relation to a term of imprisonment in respect of an offence triable either way under the law of England and Wales, “general limit in a magistrates’ court” means the limit laid down in respect of the offence by section 224(1) of the Sentencing Code (as it has effect from time to time)."
        `the enactment it points at` IS NOTHING
        `the mark`                   IS `the entry has no mark`

-- src:345 | In relation to England and Wales—
-- src:346 | (a) references (however expressed) to any relationship between two persons;
-- src:347 | (b) references to a person whose father and mother were or were not married to , or civil partners of, each other at the time of his birth; and
-- src:348 | (c) references cognate with references falling within paragraph (b) above,
-- src:349 | shall be construed in accordance with section 1 of the Family Law Reform Act 1987. [The date of the coming into force of that section]
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, Relationships (England and Wales) (src:345-349)
GIVETH A `A Schedule 1 definition`
`Schedule 1 states Relationships (England and Wales)` MEANS
    `A Schedule 1 definition` WITH
        `the terms it defines`       IS (LIST)
        `how it defines`             IS `by saying how a reference is to be construed`
        `in relation to`             IS (JUST "In relation to England and Wales")
        `what the entry says`        IS "In relation to England and Wales— (a) references (however expressed) to any relationship between two persons; (b) references to a person whose father and mother were or were not married to , or civil partners of, each other at the time of his birth; and (c) references cognate with references falling within paragraph (b) above, shall be construed in accordance with section 1 of the Family Law Reform Act 1987. [The date of the coming into force of that section]"
        `the enactment it points at` IS (JUST "section 1 of the Family Law Reform Act 1987")
        `the mark`                   IS (`the entry has a date described but not given` "The date of the coming into force of that section")

-- src:351 | In relation to Scotland—
-- src:352 | (a) references to a police force include references to the Police Service of Scotland;
-- src:353 | (b) references to a chief officer of police include references to the chief constable of the Police Service of Scotland;
-- src:354 | (c) “police authority” means the Scottish Police Authority;
-- src:355 | (d) the “police area” of the Police Service of Scotland is Scotland and references to a police force or police authority for any area include references to the Police Service of Scotland or, as the case may be, the Scottish Police Authority;
-- src:356 | (e) references to a constable or chief constable of, or appointed for, any area are to be construed as references to a constable or, as the case may be, the chief constable of, or appointed for, the Police Service of Scotland.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, Police: Scotland (src:351-356)
GIVETH A `A Schedule 1 definition`
`Schedule 1 states Police: Scotland` MEANS
    `A Schedule 1 definition` WITH
        `the terms it defines`       IS (LIST "police authority", "police area")
        `how it defines`             IS `by saying what the term means`
        `in relation to`             IS (JUST "In relation to Scotland")
        `what the entry says`        IS "In relation to Scotland— (a) references to a police force include references to the Police Service of Scotland; (b) references to a chief officer of police include references to the chief constable of the Police Service of Scotland; (c) “police authority” means the Scottish Police Authority; (d) the “police area” of the Police Service of Scotland is Scotland and references to a police force or police authority for any area include references to the Police Service of Scotland or, as the case may be, the Scottish Police Authority; (e) references to a constable or chief constable of, or appointed for, any area are to be construed as references to a constable or, as the case may be, the chief constable of, or appointed for, the Police Service of Scotland."
        `the enactment it points at` IS NOTHING
        `the mark`                   IS `the entry has no mark`

§ `The entry for an entry of the Schedule`

-- src:225 | “Act” means an Act of Parliament.
-- src:383 | “The Treaties” or “the EU Treaties” means the Treaties or EU Treaties as at immediately before IP completion day and within the meaning given by section 1(2) of the European Communities Act 1972.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 (src:225) to (src:383)
GIVEN entry IS A `Schedule 1 entry`
GIVETH A `A Schedule 1 definition`
`Schedule 1 — the definition of` entry MEANS
    CONSIDER entry
    WHEN `Act` THEN `Schedule 1 states Act`
    WHEN `Associated state` THEN `Schedule 1 states Associated state`
    WHEN `Bank of England` THEN `Schedule 1 states Bank of England`
    WHEN `Bank of Ireland` THEN `Schedule 1 states Bank of Ireland`
    WHEN `British Islands` THEN `Schedule 1 states British Islands`
    WHEN `British overseas territory` THEN `Schedule 1 states British overseas territory`
    WHEN `British possession` THEN `Schedule 1 states British possession`
    WHEN `Building regulations` THEN `Schedule 1 states Building regulations`
    WHEN `Central funds` THEN `Schedule 1 states Central funds`
    WHEN `Charity Commission` THEN `Schedule 1 states Charity Commission`
    WHEN `Church Commissioners` THEN `Schedule 1 states Church Commissioners`
    WHEN `Civil partnership` THEN `Schedule 1 states Civil partnership`
    WHEN `Colonial legislature` THEN `Schedule 1 states Colonial legislature`
    WHEN `Colony` THEN `Schedule 1 states Colony`
    WHEN `Commencement` THEN `Schedule 1 states Commencement`
    WHEN `Committed for trial (b)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Committed for trial (b)`
    WHEN `Comptroller and Auditor General` THEN `Schedule 1 states Comptroller and Auditor General`
    WHEN `Consular officer` THEN `Schedule 1 states Consular officer`
    WHEN `The Corporation Tax Acts` THEN `Schedule 1 states The Corporation Tax Acts`
    WHEN `County court (a)` THEN `Schedule 1 states County court (a)`
    WHEN `County court (b)` THEN `Schedule 1 states County court (b)`
    WHEN `Court of Appeal (a)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Court of Appeal (a)`
    WHEN `Court of Appeal (b)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Court of Appeal (b)`
    WHEN `Court of Judicature` THEN `Schedule 1 states Court of Judicature`
    WHEN `Court of summary jurisdiction` THEN `Schedule 1 states Court of summary jurisdiction`
    WHEN `Crown Court (a)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Crown Court (a)`
    WHEN `Crown Court (b)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Crown Court (b)`
    WHEN `Crown Estate Commissioners` THEN `Schedule 1 states Crown Estate Commissioners`
    WHEN `Enactment` THEN `Schedule 1 states Enactment`
    WHEN `England` THEN `Schedule 1 states England`
    WHEN `Financial year` THEN `Schedule 1 states Financial year`
    WHEN `Governor-General` THEN `Schedule 1 states Governor-General`
    WHEN `Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs` THEN `Schedule 1 states Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs`
    WHEN `High Court (a)` THEN `Schedule 1 states High Court (a)`
    WHEN `High Court (b)` THEN `Schedule 1 states High Court (b)`
    WHEN `The Immigration Acts` THEN `Schedule 1 states The Immigration Acts`
    WHEN `The Income Tax Acts` THEN `Schedule 1 states The Income Tax Acts`
    WHEN `Land` THEN `Schedule 1 states Land`
    WHEN `Lands Clauses Acts (a)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Lands Clauses Acts (a)`
    WHEN `Lands Clauses Acts (b)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Lands Clauses Acts (b)`
    WHEN `Lands Clauses Acts (c)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Lands Clauses Acts (c)`
    WHEN `Local land charges register` THEN `Schedule 1 states Local land charges register`
    WHEN `Local policing body` THEN `Schedule 1 states Local policing body`
    WHEN `London borough` THEN `Schedule 1 states London borough`
    WHEN `Lord Chancellor` THEN `Schedule 1 states Lord Chancellor`
    WHEN `Magistrates’ court (a)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Magistrates’ court (a)`
    WHEN `Magistrates’ court (b)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Magistrates’ court (b)`
    WHEN `Month` THEN `Schedule 1 states Month`
    WHEN `National Debt Commissioners` THEN `Schedule 1 states National Debt Commissioners`
    WHEN `Northern Ireland legislation` THEN `Schedule 1 states Northern Ireland legislation`
    WHEN `Oath` THEN `Schedule 1 states Oath`
    WHEN `Officer of a provider of probation services` THEN `Schedule 1 states Officer of a provider of probation services`
    WHEN `Officer of Revenue and Customs` THEN `Schedule 1 states Officer of Revenue and Customs`
    WHEN `Ordnance Map` THEN `Schedule 1 states Ordnance Map`
    WHEN `Parliamentary Election` THEN `Schedule 1 states Parliamentary Election`
    WHEN `PAYE income` THEN `Schedule 1 states PAYE income`
    WHEN `PAYE regulations` THEN `Schedule 1 states PAYE regulations`
    WHEN `Person` THEN `Schedule 1 states Person`
    WHEN `Police and crime commissioner` THEN `Schedule 1 states Police and crime commissioner`
    WHEN `Police area (a)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Police area (a)`
    WHEN `Police Service of Northern Ireland` THEN `Schedule 1 states Police Service of Northern Ireland`
    WHEN `The Privy Council` THEN `Schedule 1 states The Privy Council`
    WHEN `Provider of probation services` THEN `Schedule 1 states Provider of probation services`
    WHEN `Registered` THEN `Schedule 1 states Registered`
    WHEN `Registered medical practitioner` THEN `Schedule 1 states Registered medical practitioner`
    WHEN `Registered provider of social housing` THEN `Schedule 1 states Registered provider of social housing`
    WHEN `Rules of Court` THEN `Schedule 1 states Rules of Court`
    WHEN `Secretary of State` THEN `Schedule 1 states Secretary of State`
    WHEN `Senior Courts` THEN `Schedule 1 states Senior Courts`
    WHEN `Sent for trial` THEN `Schedule 1 states Sent for trial`
    WHEN `The Sentencing Code` THEN `Schedule 1 states The Sentencing Code`
    WHEN `Sewerage undertaker` THEN `Schedule 1 states Sewerage undertaker`
    WHEN `Sheriff` THEN `Schedule 1 states Sheriff`
    WHEN `The standard scale (a)` THEN `Schedule 1 states The standard scale (a)`
    WHEN `The standard scale (b)` THEN `Schedule 1 states The standard scale (b)`
    WHEN `The standard scale (c)` THEN `Schedule 1 states The standard scale (c)`
    WHEN `Statutory declaration` THEN `Schedule 1 states Statutory declaration`
    WHEN `Statutory maximum (a)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Statutory maximum (a)`
    WHEN `Statutory maximum (b)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Statutory maximum (b)`
    WHEN `Statutory maximum (c)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Statutory maximum (c)`
    WHEN `Supreme Court` THEN `Schedule 1 states Supreme Court`
    WHEN `The Tax Acts` THEN `Schedule 1 states The Tax Acts`
    WHEN `The Treasury` THEN `Schedule 1 states The Treasury`
    WHEN `Trust of land` THEN `Schedule 1 states Trust of land`
    WHEN `United Kingdom` THEN `Schedule 1 states United Kingdom`
    WHEN `Wales` THEN `Schedule 1 states Wales`
    WHEN `Water undertaker` THEN `Schedule 1 states Water undertaker`
    WHEN `Writing` THEN `Schedule 1 states Writing`
    WHEN `Assimilated law` THEN `Schedule 1 states Assimilated law`
    WHEN `Assimilated obligation` THEN `Schedule 1 states Assimilated obligation`
    WHEN `The Communities` THEN `Schedule 1 states The Communities`
    WHEN `E.C.S.C. Treaty` THEN `Schedule 1 states E.C.S.C. Treaty`
    WHEN `EEA agreement` THEN `Schedule 1 states EEA agreement`
    WHEN `EEA state` THEN `Schedule 1 states EEA state`
    WHEN `E.E.C. Treaty` THEN `Schedule 1 states E.E.C. Treaty`
    WHEN `Entry date` THEN `Schedule 1 states Entry date`
    WHEN `The EU` THEN `Schedule 1 states The EU`
    WHEN `EU institution` THEN `Schedule 1 states EU institution`
    WHEN `EU instrument` THEN `Schedule 1 states EU instrument`
    WHEN `Euratom` THEN `Schedule 1 states Euratom`
    WHEN `Euratom Treaty` THEN `Schedule 1 states Euratom Treaty`
    WHEN `European Court` THEN `Schedule 1 states European Court`
    WHEN `EU withdrawal agreement` THEN `Schedule 1 states EU withdrawal agreement`
    WHEN `Exit day` THEN `Schedule 1 states Exit day`
    WHEN `IP completion day` THEN `Schedule 1 states IP completion day`
    WHEN `Member` THEN `Schedule 1 states Member`
    WHEN `The Treaties` THEN `Schedule 1 states The Treaties`
    WHEN `Offences (England and Wales)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Offences (England and Wales)`
    WHEN `Relationships (England and Wales)` THEN `Schedule 1 states Relationships (England and Wales)`
    WHEN `Police: Scotland` THEN `Schedule 1 states Police: Scotland`

-- A word that Schedule 1 does not define is not covered: the lookup refuses by name.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 5 (src:17-18), Sch 1 (src:225-383): the Schedule lists the words it defines
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule 1 does not define the word` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule 1 does not define the word"

-- src:17 | 5 Definitions.
-- src:18 | In any Act, unless the contrary intention appears, words and expressions listed in Schedule 1 to this Act are to be construed according to that Schedule.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 5 (src:17-18): the words and expressions listed in Schedule 1
GIVEN word IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF `Schedule 1 entry`
`Schedule 1 — the entries that define the word` word MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF word EQUALS "Act" THEN LIST `Act`
        IF word EQUALS "affidavit" THEN LIST `Oath`
        IF word EQUALS "assimilated direct legislation" THEN LIST `Assimilated law`
        IF word EQUALS "assimilated direct minor legislation" THEN LIST `Assimilated law`
        IF word EQUALS "assimilated direct principal legislation" THEN LIST `Assimilated law`
        IF word EQUALS "Assimilated law" THEN LIST `Assimilated law`
        IF word EQUALS "Assimilated obligation" THEN LIST `Assimilated obligation`
        IF word EQUALS "Associated state" THEN LIST `Associated state`
        IF word EQUALS "Bank of England" THEN LIST `Bank of England`
        IF word EQUALS "Bank of Ireland" THEN LIST `Bank of Ireland`
        IF word EQUALS "British Islands" THEN LIST `British Islands`
        IF word EQUALS "British overseas territory" THEN LIST `British overseas territory`
        IF word EQUALS "British possession" THEN LIST `British possession`
        IF word EQUALS "Building regulations" THEN LIST `Building regulations`
        IF word EQUALS "Central funds" THEN LIST `Central funds`
        IF word EQUALS "Charity Commission" THEN LIST `Charity Commission`
        IF word EQUALS "Church Commissioners" THEN LIST `Church Commissioners`
        IF word EQUALS "Civil partnership" THEN LIST `Civil partnership`
        IF word EQUALS "Coal and Steel Community" THEN LIST `Euratom`
        IF word EQUALS "Colonial legislature" THEN LIST `Colonial legislature`
        IF word EQUALS "Colony" THEN LIST `Colony`
        IF word EQUALS "Commencement" THEN LIST `Commencement`
        IF word EQUALS "Committed for trial" THEN LIST `Committed for trial (b)`
        IF word EQUALS "Comptroller and Auditor General" THEN LIST `Comptroller and Auditor General`
        IF word EQUALS "Consular officer" THEN LIST `Consular officer`
        IF word EQUALS "County court" THEN LIST `County court (a)`, `County court (b)`
        IF word EQUALS "Court of Appeal" THEN LIST `Court of Appeal (a)`, `Court of Appeal (b)`
        IF word EQUALS "Court of Judicature" THEN LIST `Court of Judicature`
        IF word EQUALS "Court of summary jurisdiction" THEN LIST `Court of summary jurisdiction`
        IF word EQUALS "Crown Court" THEN LIST `Crown Court (a)`, `Crown Court (b)`
        IF word EQUALS "Crown Estate Commissioners" THEN LIST `Crown Estate Commissioners`
        IF word EQUALS "E.C.S.C. Treaty" THEN LIST `E.C.S.C. Treaty`
        IF word EQUALS "E.E.C. Treaty" THEN LIST `E.E.C. Treaty`
        IF word EQUALS "Economic Community" THEN LIST `Euratom`
        IF word EQUALS "EEA agreement" THEN LIST `EEA agreement`
        IF word EQUALS "EEA state" THEN LIST `EEA state`
        IF word EQUALS "Enactment" THEN LIST `Enactment`
        IF word EQUALS "England" THEN LIST `England`
        IF word EQUALS "Entry date" THEN LIST `Entry date`
        IF word EQUALS "EU institution" THEN LIST `EU institution`
        IF word EQUALS "EU instrument" THEN LIST `EU instrument`
        IF word EQUALS "EU withdrawal agreement" THEN LIST `EU withdrawal agreement`
        IF word EQUALS "Euratom" THEN LIST `Euratom`
        IF word EQUALS "Euratom Treaty" THEN LIST `Euratom Treaty`
        IF word EQUALS "European Court" THEN LIST `European Court`
        IF word EQUALS "Exit day" THEN LIST `Exit day`
        IF word EQUALS "Financial year" THEN LIST `Financial year`
        IF word EQUALS "general limit in a magistrates’ court" THEN LIST `Offences (England and Wales)`
        IF word EQUALS "Governor" THEN LIST `Governor-General`
        IF word EQUALS "Governor-General" THEN LIST `Governor-General`
        IF word EQUALS "Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs" THEN LIST `Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs`
        IF word EQUALS "High Court" THEN LIST `High Court (a)`, `High Court (b)`
        IF word EQUALS "indictable" THEN LIST `Offences (England and Wales)`
        IF word EQUALS "indictable offence" THEN LIST `Offences (England and Wales)`
        IF word EQUALS "inner London borough" THEN LIST `London borough`
        IF word EQUALS "IP completion day" THEN LIST `IP completion day`
        IF word EQUALS "Land" THEN LIST `Land`
        IF word EQUALS "Lands Clauses Acts" THEN LIST `Lands Clauses Acts (a)`, `Lands Clauses Acts (b)`, `Lands Clauses Acts (c)`
        IF word EQUALS "legislature" THEN LIST `Colonial legislature`
        IF word EQUALS "Local land charges register" THEN LIST `Local land charges register`
        IF word EQUALS "Local policing body" THEN LIST `Local policing body`
        IF word EQUALS "London borough" THEN LIST `London borough`
        IF word EQUALS "Lord Chancellor" THEN LIST `Lord Chancellor`
        IF word EQUALS "Magistrates’ court" THEN LIST `Magistrates’ court (a)`, `Magistrates’ court (b)`
        IF word EQUALS "Member" THEN LIST `Member`
        IF word EQUALS "Month" THEN LIST `Month`
        IF word EQUALS "National Debt Commissioners" THEN LIST `National Debt Commissioners`
        IF word EQUALS "Northern Ireland legislation" THEN LIST `Northern Ireland legislation`
        IF word EQUALS "Oath" THEN LIST `Oath`
        IF word EQUALS "offence triable either way" THEN LIST `Offences (England and Wales)`
        IF word EQUALS "Officer of a provider of probation services" THEN LIST `Officer of a provider of probation services`
        IF word EQUALS "Officer of Revenue and Customs" THEN LIST `Officer of Revenue and Customs`
        IF word EQUALS "Ordnance Map" THEN LIST `Ordnance Map`
        IF word EQUALS "outer London borough" THEN LIST `London borough`
        IF word EQUALS "Parliamentary Election" THEN LIST `Parliamentary Election`
        IF word EQUALS "PAYE income" THEN LIST `PAYE income`
        IF word EQUALS "PAYE regulations" THEN LIST `PAYE regulations`
        IF word EQUALS "Person" THEN LIST `Person`
        IF word EQUALS "Police and crime commissioner" THEN LIST `Police and crime commissioner`
        IF word EQUALS "Police area" THEN LIST `Police area (a)`
        IF word EQUALS "police area" THEN LIST `Police: Scotland`
        IF word EQUALS "police authority" THEN LIST `Police: Scotland`
        IF word EQUALS "Police Service of Northern Ireland" THEN LIST `Police Service of Northern Ireland`
        IF word EQUALS "Police Service of Northern Ireland Reserve" THEN LIST `Police Service of Northern Ireland`
        IF word EQUALS "private registered provider of social housing" THEN LIST `Registered provider of social housing`
        IF word EQUALS "Provider of probation services" THEN LIST `Provider of probation services`
        IF word EQUALS "Registered" THEN LIST `Registered`
        IF word EQUALS "Registered medical practitioner" THEN LIST `Registered medical practitioner`
        IF word EQUALS "Registered provider of social housing" THEN LIST `Registered provider of social housing`
        IF word EQUALS "Rules of Court" THEN LIST `Rules of Court`
        IF word EQUALS "Secretary of State" THEN LIST `Secretary of State`
        IF word EQUALS "Senior Courts" THEN LIST `Senior Courts`
        IF word EQUALS "Sent for trial" THEN LIST `Sent for trial`
        IF word EQUALS "Sewerage undertaker" THEN LIST `Sewerage undertaker`
        IF word EQUALS "Sheriff" THEN LIST `Sheriff`
        IF word EQUALS "Statutory declaration" THEN LIST `Statutory declaration`
        IF word EQUALS "Statutory maximum" THEN LIST `Statutory maximum (a)`, `Statutory maximum (b)`, `Statutory maximum (c)`
        IF word EQUALS "summary" THEN LIST `Offences (England and Wales)`
        IF word EQUALS "summary conviction" THEN LIST `Court of summary jurisdiction`
        IF word EQUALS "Summary Jurisdiction Acts" THEN LIST `Court of summary jurisdiction`
        IF word EQUALS "summary offence" THEN LIST `Offences (England and Wales)`
        IF word EQUALS "Supreme Court" THEN LIST `Supreme Court`
        IF word EQUALS "swear" THEN LIST `Oath`
        IF word EQUALS "The Communities" THEN LIST `The Communities`
        IF word EQUALS "The Corporation Tax Acts" THEN LIST `The Corporation Tax Acts`
        IF word EQUALS "The EU" THEN LIST `The EU`
        IF word EQUALS "the EU Treaties" THEN LIST `The Treaties`
        IF word EQUALS "the European Union" THEN LIST `The EU`
        IF word EQUALS "The Immigration Acts" THEN LIST `The Immigration Acts`
        IF word EQUALS "The Income Tax Acts" THEN LIST `The Income Tax Acts`
        IF word EQUALS "The Privy Council" THEN LIST `The Privy Council`
        IF word EQUALS "The Sentencing Code" THEN LIST `The Sentencing Code`
        IF word EQUALS "The standard scale" THEN LIST `The standard scale (a)`, `The standard scale (b)`, `The standard scale (c)`
        IF word EQUALS "The Tax Acts" THEN LIST `The Tax Acts`
        IF word EQUALS "The Treasury" THEN LIST `The Treasury`
        IF word EQUALS "The Treaties" THEN LIST `The Treaties`
        IF word EQUALS "triable either way" THEN LIST `Offences (England and Wales)`
        IF word EQUALS "Trust of land" THEN LIST `Trust of land`
        IF word EQUALS "trustees of land" THEN LIST `Trust of land`
        IF word EQUALS "United Kingdom" THEN LIST `United Kingdom`
        IF word EQUALS "Wales" THEN LIST `Wales`
        IF word EQUALS "Water undertaker" THEN LIST `Water undertaker`
        IF word EQUALS "Writing" THEN LIST `Writing`
        OTHERWISE `Schedule 1 does not define the word`

§ `The bracket, Schedule 2 paragraph 4 and Schedule 2 Part II`

-- src:413 | 4 (1) Subject to the following provisions of this paragraph—
-- src:414 | (a) paragraphs of Schedule 1 at the end of which a year or date . . . is specified or described apply, so far as applicable, to Acts passed on or after the date, or after the year, so specified or described: and
-- src:415 | (b) paragraphs of that Schedule at the end of which no year or date is specified or described apply, so far as applicable, to Acts passed at any time.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 4(1) (src:413-415): a date that the bracket describes and does not give is asked as an input
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule 1 describes the date in the bracket and does not give it, so the caller must say what date it names` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule 1 describes the date in the bracket and does not give it, so the caller must say what date it names"

@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 4(1) (src:413-415)
GIVEN mark IS A `Mark of a Schedule 1 entry`
      `the date the described bracket names` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Mark at the end of a Schedule 1 paragraph`
`Schedule 2 para 4(1) reads the mark of the entry as` mark `the date the described bracket names` MEANS
    CONSIDER mark
    WHEN `the entry has no mark` THEN `no year or date is specified`
    WHEN `the entry has a year` y THEN `a year is specified` y
    WHEN `the entry has a date` d THEN `a date is specified` d
    WHEN `the entry has a date described but not given` words THEN
        CONSIDER `the date the described bracket names`
        WHEN JUST d THEN `a date is specified` d
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `Schedule 1 describes the date in the bracket and does not give it, so the caller must say what date it names`

-- Schedule 2 Part II names the expressions of Schedule 1 that reach subordinate legislation made before the commencement (paras 6 to 8).
-- src:429 | 6 Sections 4(a), 9 and 19(1), and so much of Schedule 1 as defines the following expressions, namely—
-- src:431 | England;
-- src:432 | Local land charges register and appropriate local land charges register;
-- src:433 | in relation to Scotland, expressions relating to the police;
-- src:434 | United Kingdom;
-- src:435 | Wales,
-- src:436 | apply to subordinate legislation made at any time before the commencement of this Act as they apply to Acts passed at that time.
-- src:437 | 7 The definition in Schedule 1 of “county court”, in relation to England and Wales, applies to Orders in Council made after the year 1846.
-- src:438 | 8 The definition in Schedule 1 of “enactment”, in so far as it relates to assimilated direct legislation, applies to subordinate legislation made at any time before the commencement of this Act as it applies to Acts passed at that time.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 Part II paras 6 to 8 (src:429-438)
GIVEN entry IS A `Schedule 1 entry`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Expression that Schedule 2 Part II applies`
`the expression of Schedule 2 Part II that the entry states` entry MEANS
    CONSIDER entry
    WHEN `England` THEN JUST `England`
    WHEN `Local land charges register` THEN JUST `Local land charges register and appropriate local land charges register`
    WHEN `Police: Scotland` THEN JUST `in relation to Scotland, expressions relating to the police`
    WHEN `United Kingdom` THEN JUST `United Kingdom`
    WHEN `Wales` THEN JUST `Wales`
    WHEN `County court (a)` THEN JUST `county court, in relation to England and Wales`
    WHEN `Enactment` THEN JUST `enactment, in so far as it relates to assimilated direct legislation`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Section 5: the word is construed according to Schedule 1`

@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 5 (src:17-18): "unless the contrary intention appears"
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 5 construes the word according to Schedule 1 unless a contrary intention appears, and one appears` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 5 construes the word according to Schedule 1 unless a contrary intention appears, and one appears"

-- src:103 | (1) This Act applies to itself, to any Act passed after the commencement of this Act (subject , in the case of section 20(2A) to (6), to the provision made in section 20(2A) or (3) and, in the case of section 20A, to the provision made in that section) and, to the extent specified in Part I of Schedule 2, to Acts passed before the commencement of this Act.
-- src:107 | (1) The provisions of this Act, except sections 1 to 3 and 4(b), apply, so far as applicable and unless the contrary intention appears, to subordinate legislation made after the commencement of this Act and, to the extent specified in Part II of Schedule 2, to subordinate legislation made before the commencement of this Act, as they apply to Acts.
-- Whether the entry reaches the enactment: an enactment made on or after the commencement takes the whole of Schedule 1 (ss 22(1), 23(1)), an Act passed before it takes
-- the entry according to its bracket (Sch 2 para 4(1)), and subordinate legislation made before it takes only the expressions that Part II of Schedule 2 names.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 5 (src:17-18); s 22(1) (src:103); s 23(1) (src:107); Sch 2 para 4(1) (src:413-415); Sch 2 Part II paras 6 to 8 (src:429-438)
GIVEN e IS AN `An enactment`
      entry IS A `Schedule 1 entry`
      `the date the described bracket names` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the entry reaches the enactment` e entry `the date the described bracket names` MEANS
    IF   `the day is on or after the commencement of the Interpretation Act 1978` (e's `the day it was passed or made`)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER e's `its kind`
         WHEN `an Act` THEN
             `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` e (`Schedule 2 para 4(1) reads the mark of the entry as` ((`Schedule 1 — the definition of` entry)'s `the mark`) `the date the described bracket names`)
         WHEN `subordinate legislation` THEN
             CONSIDER `the expression of Schedule 2 Part II that the entry states` entry
             WHEN JUST x THEN `Schedule 2 Part II — the definition applies to subordinate legislation made before the commencement, on` x (e's `the day it was passed or made`)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- src:17 | 5 Definitions.
-- src:18 | In any Act, unless the contrary intention appears, words and expressions listed in Schedule 1 to this Act are to be construed according to that Schedule.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 5 (src:17-18)
GIVEN e IS AN `An enactment`
      entry IS A `Schedule 1 entry`
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the described bracket names` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `A Schedule 1 definition`
`section 5 construes the word in the enactment according to Schedule 1` e entry `the contrary intention appears` `the date the described bracket names` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contrary intention appears`
            THEN `section 5 construes the word according to Schedule 1 unless a contrary intention appears, and one appears`
        IF `the entry reaches the enactment` e entry `the date the described bracket names`
            THEN JUST (`Schedule 1 — the definition of` entry)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

